    "result_text": "The build succeeds. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the disposable-domain email blocklist for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Where the check lives:** `RequireOwnerFields` already binds, syntactically validates, and normalizes the email (trim + lowercase). I added the blocklist check right after syntactic validation, operating on the normalized (lower-cased) domain so casing/whitespace variants are caught too. It extracts the domain after the last `@` and rejects if it's in the blocklist set `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}`.\n\n**New files (mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailException` trio):**\n- `escalation/DisposableEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it appears in `throws`).\n- `escalation/DisposableEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DisposableEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Edited:** `RequireOwnerFields.java` \u2014 added the domain set, the check, and the `throws DisposableEmailException` clause.\n\nThe valid-email path is unchanged (a non-blocklisted address is still normalized and stored), and an absent/blank email is still accepted. `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
